WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.259
D P O.

2
00:00:01.259 --> 00:00:03.633
Direct preference optimization.

3
00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:06.631
RLHF is the concept you explain.

4
00:00:06.631 --> 00:00:09.667
DPO is the trainer you actually run.

5
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:12.033
Here's the insight.

6
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:14.667
You don't need to train a separate reward model.

7
00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:17.267
And you don't need to run reinforcement learning.

8
00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:21.733
If you have preference pairs, you can optimize the policy directly on them.

9
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:29.167
Each training row has three parts: a prompt, a chosen response that people liked, and a rejected one.

10
00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:32.967
DPO raises the probability of the chosen response.

11
00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:38.633
And lowers the probability of the rejected one, both measured against a frozen reference.

12
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:41.300
Compare the two approaches.

13
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.900
RLHF needs four models.

14
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.300
DPO needs two.

15
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.269
RLHF uses unstable reinforcement learning.

16
00:00:49.269 --> 00:00:53.200
DPO trains like ordinary supervised learning.

17
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.633
RLHF builds a reward model first.

18
00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:57.867
DPO skips it.

19
00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:01.667
So DPO is cheaper, more stable, and the current default.

20
00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:04.067
Here it is in code.

21
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:08.267
The dataset holds a prompt, a chosen and a rejected reply.

22
00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.609
No reward model, no value head.

23
00:01:10.609 --> 00:01:14.233
Beta controls how hard we push away from the reference.

24
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:19.567
Imagine Mission Control logs a thumbs up or down on every answer.

25
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:26.500
Six months in, you have thousands of pairs: the answer users accepted, and the regeneration they rejected.

26
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.933
With DPOTrainer, that becomes a weekend project that tunes the model toward what your users prefer.

27
00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:34.948
Let's recap.

28
00:01:34.948 --> 00:01:37.800
DPO learns directly from preference pairs.

29
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.400
No reward model and no PPO.

30
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.600
Two models and stable training.

31
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.776
And beta controls the push.

32
00:01:44.776 --> 00:01:47.000
Next up: supervised fine-tuning.
